   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch4/q4",
   "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:110mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/pmt/pure-core-2-ch4/q04-fig-1.png\" alt=\"Figure 3: axes x and y with origin O; the curve C rising from the left above the x-axis through the y-axis to the point P; the line l touches C at P and meets the x-axis at Q; the region R between the curve, the axes and the line l is shaded; labelled &quot;Diagram not to scale&quot;\"></figure><p>Figure 3 shows a sketch of part of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=3^x\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> and has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,9)\"></span>.</p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> is a tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>. The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> cuts the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Find the exact value of the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>The finite region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 3, is bounded by the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span>. This region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is rotated through 360° about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Use integration to find the exact value of the volume of the solid generated.</p><p>Give your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{p}{q}\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> are exact constants.</p><p>[<em>You may assume the formula <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=\\frac13\\pi r^2h\"></span> for the volume of a cone.</em>]</p><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol>",
